  "aboutTooltip": "About",
  "aboutDescription": "Flashes Allwinner T507 / T527 boards over the FEL/EFEX USB protocol — an open-source alternative to PhoenixSuit.\n\nA board is taken from FEL into EFEX using primers extracted from the image itself, then the partition table, every partition, BOOT1 and BOOT0 are written.",

  "troubleshootTooltip": "Troubleshoot",
  "troubleshootTitle": "Board not detected on Windows?",
  "troubleshootIntro": "The board can look completely normal in Device Manager and still be invisible to this app. That happens when the Microsoft default driver is bound instead of WinUSB — libusb can't open the device at all in that case. Running a command against it looks like this:",
  "troubleshootStep1": "Keep the board connected in FEL (or EFEX) mode.",
  "troubleshootStep2": "Run Zadig (zadig.akeo.ie) — no admin rights needed.",
  "troubleshootStep3": "Turn on Options → List All Devices. Without it, a device that already has a driver bound won't show up in the list.",
  "troubleshootStep4": "Find the device by VID 1f3a / PID efe8, set the driver to WinUSB, and click Replace Driver.",
  "troubleshootStep5": "Check Device Manager again — it should now be listed under \"Universal Serial Bus devices\".",
  "troubleshootNote": "Once bound, it's recognised automatically after that, including across reboots.",

